==============================================================================
## Scaling laws: fit cmix and smix vs (log x)^a, x^b
==============================================================================
  [divisor] cmix ~ x^0.145 or (log x)^0.674
  [divisor] smix ~ x^0.043 or (log x)^0.191
  [coprime] cmix ~ x^0.244 or (log x)^1.054
  [coprime] smix ~ x^0.000 or (log x)^-0.000
  [cayley_unit] cmix ~ x^0.789 or (log x)^3.632
  [cayley_unit] smix ~ x^0.414 or (log x)^1.907

## Polylog test
If smix ~ (log x)^a for small a, Szegedy is polylog-mixing on this graph.
If smix ~ x^b for b > 0, Szegedy is poly(x)-mixing -- no polylog opening.